description:
Roles and functions of clinical laboratories and practitioners; professionalism and ethics; 
educational methodology and training; professional and interpersonal communication; 
behavioral aspects of management; leadership styles and management theory; team-building; 
legal issues related to employment; recruitment, interview and selection of personnel; 
organizational culture and behavioral change; laboratory operations; safety, governmental 
regulations, standards and compliance; marketing, outreach, and business plan; budget, cost 
analysis, reimbursement; critical pathways, decision-making, test utilization; performance 
improvement, quality assessment; risk management, evidence-based laboratory medicine.
